    has been implemented but hadn't been fully tested & engaged. What started
    off as a 'feature enablement' effort resulted in following changes, many
    arising during review discussions:
    
    - Externalize num_normal_bg_threads and num_memtable_bg_threads as new
      fields in splinter_config{}. A requirement is that both have to be
      non-zero for task-system to successfully come up w/ bg-threads enabled.
    
    - Minor adjustments are done to task system initialization to
      manage the order in which background threads are started up.
    
    - Tightened some checks while task-system is bootstrapped and while
      threads are created to ensure that we don't overrun limit of MAX_THREADS
      that can be concurrently started, including thread-0 for the main program.
      Attempt to start a thread beyond this limit will fail with
      STATUS_BUSY ('Resource temporarily unavailable') error.
    
    - Added new cases in task_system_test to verify the new variation that
      the task system test case could, optionally, be exercised with
      --num-bg-threads | --num-memtable-bg-threads arguments.
    
    - Enhanced config_parse() to recognize these two new options.
      Added a case to test.sh to exercise the task_system_test with background
      threads. This change now sets us up to invoke other functional tests enabled
      with bg-threads. That change to test.sh can be added in the future.
    
    - Add several new unit-tests exercising this capability and added couple of
      calls to test.sh to exercise some functional tests with bg-threads.

