    Minor updates to clang-format rules, and coding style changes
    
    This commit introduces minor additions to clang-format rules as
    they are defined in the .clang-format file, which is per v10 of
    clang-format. Specifically, the couple of new formatting styles
    introduced by this change are:
    
    1. Brace for body of case: statement will begin on a new line,
       as opposed to being on the same line following the case: LABEL.
    
       Rule: The nested definition of "AfterCaseLabel:  true"
             under BraceWrapping: rules introduces this behavior.
    
       New format will be like: (expected to improve readability)
        case LABEL:
        {
            < some code >
        }
    
    2. Multi-line conditional statements for if(), for() or while()
       will have their start { appear on a new-line indented under
       the start of the conditional. This improves readability of
       densely packed if(), for(), while() constructs with muti-line
       conditional logic tests.
    
       Rule: The nested definition of "AfterControlStatement: MultiLine"
             under BraceWrapping: rules introduces this behavior.
    
       New format will be like:
        if ( < Some long multi-line >
            && <comment that spills over to new lines> )
        {
            < body of block >
        }
    
        NOTE: Single line if(), for() conditionals continue to have the
              start { follow the conditional on the same line.
    
    Additional minor refactoring done:
     - In few places enclose single-line bodies of if()/else() blocks in { }
       (All new code should conform to this existing rule.)
     - In couple of places, enclose sub-parts of complex expressions in ( )
       to improve readability. (Some of these are superfluous but including
       them clarifies to the reader exactly the priority of the terms.)
     - Some refactoring in new BTree code multi-line comment blocks.
     - Delete blank lines in multi-line prolog, to keep the prolog compact.
     - Delete blank line between function prolog and start of the function
       definition. In some places delete blank line between multi-line comment
       blocks and body of code. Both changes work towards reducing scope for
       dangling comment blocks, and to ensure that the comment block / prolog
       is tightly bound to the code-section it refers to.

