Author: Alex Conway <aconway@vmware.com>
Date:   Fri Aug 27 14:11:08 2021 -0700

    Fix race between branch_dec_ref and range_iterators
    
    Re-adds coordination between branch_dec_ref and range_iterators. Prior
    to #65 this was handling by using read/write locks on the meta_page of
    the meta_head. This is not ideal, because those write locks interfere
    with tiered memory transactions.
    
    Coordination is achieved in this commit by overloading the ref count of
    the meta head. A range query can "block" dec_refs on the mini_allocator
    by increasing the ref count and "unblock" by decrementing it again.
    mini_keyed_dec_ref callers must first wait for the ref count to go to
    AL_ONE_REF before continuing, after which they are guaranteed that no
    range queries can intersect their dec_ref range.

